{
  "name": "ALDH kinetics: acetaldehyde oxidation by human ALDH2",
  "version": "2",
  "description": "Aldehyde dehydrogenase, mitochondrial from Homo sapiens converts acetaldehyde to acetate. Formation of NADH followed photometrically at 340 nm; the decrease of acetaldehyde derived from it. Three starting concentrations spanning K_m (0.5, 1, 3 µM, K_m 1), 11 time points each over 20 min.\n\nSynthetic teaching dataset: the numbers come from a Michaelis-Menten simulation with added noise, not from a bench. The chemical and biological identifiers are real — the reaction from Rhea RHEA:25294, the enzyme from UniProt P05091.",
